## HOW TO STRUCTURE EVERY SINGLE CHANGE

Pattern — always follow this shape:

```kotlin
fun doSomething() {
    when {
        IS_WINDOWS -> {
            // existing Windows code — DO NOT TOUCH
        }
        IS_LINUX -> {
            // new Linux code here
        }
        else -> {
            // safe no-op or: println("Unsupported OS")
        }
    }
}
```

If existing code is already inside `if (isWindows) { }`,
do NOT restructure it. Just add `else if (IS_LINUX) { }`
directly after it. Do not touch the if-block itself.

