## LINUX REPLACEMENT MAP

Use these replacements exactly. Do not improvise.

### Firewall rules
```
Windows: netsh advfirewall / New-NetFirewallRule (PowerShell)
Linux:   ProcessBuilder("pkexec", "iptables", "-A", "OUTPUT",
             "-p", "tcp", "-d", domain, "-j", "DROP").start()
         Fallback: ProcessBuilder("sudo", "iptables", ...)
         Wrap in try/catch — skip silently if no root access.
```

### Kill a process by name
```
Windows: taskkill /F /IM process.exe
Linux:   ProcessHandle.allProcesses()
           .filter { it.info().command()
               .orElse("").contains(name) }
           .forEach { it.destroyForcibly() }
```

### Foreground window detection (SetWinEventHook / WinEventHook.kt)
```
Windows: SetWinEventHook via JNA
Linux:   Poll active window using xdotool every 500ms:
           ProcessBuilder("xdotool", "getactivewindow",
               "getwindowname").start()
         On Wayland: xdotool won't work. Poll /proc/*/cmdline
         instead to find the foreground process.
         Add comment:
           // Linux X11: uses xdotool polling (500ms)
           // Linux Wayland: xdotool unavailable, falling
           //   back to /proc polling — limited accuracy
```

### Autostart on login
```
Windows: HKCU Run key (WindowsStartupManager.kt)
Linux:   Write to ~/.config/autostart/focusflow.desktop
         Content of that file:
           [Desktop Entry]
           Type=Application
           Name=FocusFlow
           Exec=/path/to/focusflow
           X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true
         Use System.getProperty("user.home") for the path.
         Add Linux branch inside WindowsStartupManager.kt —
         do NOT create a new manager file.
```

### Hosts file blocking
```
Windows: Write to C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts
Linux:   Write to /etc/hosts (same format, same path concept)
         Use: ProcessBuilder("pkexec", "tee", "-a", "/etc/hosts")
         This is already almost cross-platform — just guard
         the path with IS_LINUX and use pkexec for the write.
```

### Taskbar hide/show (FocusLauncherService)
```
Windows: Hide taskbar via Win32 calls
Linux:   Attempt to hide panels:
           ProcessBuilder("xdotool", "search",
               "--class", "panel").start()
         If the command fails or returns nothing, skip silently.
         Add comment:
           // Linux kiosk: panel hiding is DE-specific.
           // Works on some GNOME/XFCE configs, not all.
           // Manual setup may be needed.
```

### Notifications
```
Windows: Balloon / toast notifications
Linux:   ProcessBuilder("notify-send", "FocusFlow", message)
           .start()
         Wrap in try/catch — skip if notify-send not installed.
```

### App/process discovery (InstalledAppsScanner.kt)
```
Windows: Registry + running process scan
Linux:   Read /usr/share/applications/*.desktop files.
         Parse Name= and Exec= fields from each file.
         Also scan /proc/*/cmdline for running processes.
```

### Nuclear Mode (NuclearMode.kt)
```
Windows: Blocks 30+ escape routes
Linux:   Block equivalent escape routes:
         - Kill: gnome-terminal, konsole, xfce4-terminal,
                 xterm if launched by the user session
         - Block via iptables DROP on loopback if needed
         - Disable Ctrl+Alt+T via gsettings if GNOME:
             ProcessBuilder("gsettings", "set",
               "org.gnome.settings-daemon.plugins.media-keys",
               "terminal", "[]").start()
         Add comment:
           // Linux Nuclear: partial coverage.
           // Some DEs need manual extension.
```

