No change needed.
javax.sound.sampled works on Linux via ALSA/PulseAudio.
Add IS_LINUX block with:
  println("SoundAversion: using ALSA/PulseAudio on Linux")
```

### Database (Database.kt / SQLite)
```
No change needed.
sqlite-jdbc is fully cross-platform. Leave it alone.
```

### Compose UI (all screens)
```
No change needed.
Compose Multiplatform renders via Skia on Linux.
No platform code required in UI files.
```

### Backup paths (BackupService / AutoBackupService)
```
Windows: %APPDATA%\FocusFlow\backups
Linux:   ~/.local/share/FocusFlow/backups
         Use:
           System.getProperty("user.home") +
             "/.local/share/FocusFlow/backups"
         Guard with IS_LINUX.
```

### System tray (SystemTrayManager.kt)
```
java.awt.SystemTray works on Linux with most DEs
but may fail silently on Wayland.
Wrap the entire tray init in try/catch.
Add comment:
  // Linux: SystemTray may not work on pure Wayland.
  // Failing silently — tray is optional on Linux.
```

### Crash recovery shutdown hook
```
Already cross-platform via Runtime.addShutdownHook.
BUT: the taskbar restore call inside it is Windows-only.
Add IS_LINUX branch:
  Attempt to restore panels via:
    ProcessBuilder("xdotool", "search", "--class",
        "panel", "windowmap").start()
  Wrap in try/catch.
```

### Process safe whitelist (FocusLauncherService)
```
Windows: 55+ whitelisted Win32 processes
Linux:   Add to the whitelist:
           "Xorg", "Xwayland", "pipewire", "pulseaudio",
           "wireplumber", "dbus-daemon", "systemd",
           "gdm", "gdm3", "sddm", "lightdm",
           "at-spi-bus-launcher", "ibus-daemon"
         Add these alongside the existing Windows entries.
         Do not remove any Windows entries.
```

